title: "Who Is Cloning All of My Repositories? An Exploration of 598 Daily Clone Events Across Six Public Repositories From Exactly 8,372 Recorded Clone Events ÷ 14 Days"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: "McCoy"
    given-names: "Taylor"
date-released: 2026-10-19
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tmccoy678/github-clone-traffic-investigation"
abstract: >-
  A descriptive case study of 8,372 GitHub-counted clone events across six public
  repositories in a 14-day window. The evidence supports selective scheduled and
  push-triggered automated collection without identifying a particular actor.
